{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-10-03T09:32:19.350Z","data":{"text":"Done. All acceptance lines are implemented and both the task verify and the proposal's `pnpm verify` exit 0.\n\nSummary of changes:\n\n- **`src/cli/plan.ts`**: `PlanCommandOptions` now extends `CommandInputs` (dropping its own `cwd`); `planCommand` uses `resolveInputs` for `cwd`, `config()`, `stdout`, and `stderr`. `--print` writes through `inputs.stdout`, the handoff writes through a local `writePromptHandoff(..., stdout)`, and `createChange`/`createQueueChange` receive `inputs.stdout` only for `--session`. `prepareQueueSelection` receives `inputs.stderr`.\n- **`src/cli/plan-queue.ts`**: moved `writePromptHandoff` out to its only caller; `prepareQueueSelection` takes an optional `stderr` writer (default `processStderr`) and writes the notice plus `\\n`; `createChange`/`createQueueChange` take `output: Writer | null` and write the two created lines with `\\n`.\n- **`tests/command-inputs-plan.test.ts`** (new): compares `osq plan --next --print` through `runCliCaptured` against a direct call on a freshly reset copy of the same project, and asserts a handoff run writes its line to the passed `stdout`.\n- **`tests/plan-command-error.test.ts`**: reads the incomplete-coverage notice from a passed `stderr` writer instead of `console.error`.\n\nResult written to `openspec/changes/142-command-inputs/.run/results/10.md`."}}
